 "comment": "A name two masters share stays in the index. Sigma Trading (a creditor) and SIGMA-TRADING (a debtor) have the same words in the same order, so the name is shared and bound to no master; a third party, Sigma, is a shorter name that lies inside it. s01 pays Beta Stores from Bank A and its narration names Sigma Trading: the shared name is found (and listed for none), so Sigma inside it is dropped as nested and s01 is not listed. s02 names only Sigma, so Sigma is found as a plain name and s02 is listed. A port that dropped the shared name from the index would list s01 for Sigma.",
